    </div>
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is EU GSP and how does it benefit Luxembourg imports?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">EU GSP provides duty-free access for Bangladesh garment exports under the EBA arrangement. Most apparel categories enter Luxembourg with zero customs duty.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How long does shipping from Bangladesh to Luxembourg take?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Luxembourg's lack of a coastline means containers typically arrive at Antwerp or Rotterdam first, then continue by road or rail to reach Luxembourg City—28-33 days in total, with the final inland stretch adding 3-5 days on top of the ocean crossing. Add 30-45 days of production time before the goods even ship.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Do you meet Luxembourg's sustainability requirements?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We maintain GOTS organic cotton and GRS recycled materials certifications, providing complete sustainability documentation for Luxembourg market compliance.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What documents do I need to import to Luxembourg?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Required documents include commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, and EU GSP proof of origin. We also provide REACH compliance certificates.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can one order cover Luxembourg plus neighbouring markets?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes — this is actually the most common pattern we see. We can prepare documentation covering combined distribution into Luxembourg, Belgium, France, and Germany from a single order and shipment.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How do you ensure fabric consistency across production runs?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Boutique and premium retail buyers, who typically order smaller runs, treat dye-lot matching as a baseline expectation rather than an upsell. So we retain the original approved lab dip and check every run against it with a spectrophotometer — not by eye — flagging anything past tolerance before it ships.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
